id: ops-042o
title: "Security: repository-host check matches too loosely (notgithub.com accepted as GitHub)"
description: "Reported by Sourcery. scripts/verify-release-completeness.ts:117 treats a repository string as a GitHub slug when it merely contains github or github.com anywhere, so https://notgithub.com/owner/name or https://evil.example/github:owner/name is accepted and the verifier queries the wrong repository. Parse the URL and require hostname === github.com exactly, handling the documented SSH (git@github.com:owner/name) and shorthand (github:owner/name) forms separately and explicitly."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-31T11:49:08.758Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T11:52:06.317Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T11:52:06.304Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T11:52:06.304Z"
author: pi-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T11:51:55.973Z",pi-agent,"Fix: Replaced the loose regex (/(?:github\\.com|github)[:/].../) with strict URL parsing. The HTTPS form is parsed with new URL and requires hostname === 'github.com' exactly. The SSH (git@github.com:owner/name) and shorthand (github:owner/name) forms are matched with anchored patterns that require the host literally. Hostile inputs like https://notgithub.com/o/n and https://evil.example/github:o/n are rejected. Revert-proof: test 'repoSlugFromUrl rejects hostile hosts that merely contain github and accepts valid GitHub forms' fails RED when the old substring regex is restored."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  scripts/verify-release-completeness.ts,project
  test/verify-release-completeness.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,path,scope,note}:
  "PM_PATH=/tmp/pm-test PM_GLOBAL_PATH=/tmp/pm-test-g node --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects hostile hosts\" test/verify-release-completeness.test.ts",test/verify-release-completeness.test.ts,project,repoSlugFromUrl rejects hostile hosts that merely contain 'github' and accepts valid GitHub forms
close_reason: "Fixed: repository-host check requires hostname === github.com exactly"
body: ""
